  "bodyHtml": "<br/>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout_warn\" theme=\"⚠️\"><span class=\"callout-icon\">⚠️</span><h3 class=\"heading heading-3 header-scroll\"><div class=\"heading-anchor anchor waypoint\" id=\"updated-terminology\"></div><div class=\"heading-text\">Updated Terminology</div><a aria-label=\"Skip link to Updated Terminology\" class=\"heading-anchor-icon fa fa-regular fa-anchor\" href=\"#updated-terminology\"></a></h3><p>Collections are now called Receives. These <code class=\"rdmd-code lang- theme-undefined\" data-lang=\"\">/receive</code> endpoints replace the legacy <code class=\"rdmd-code lang- theme-undefined\" data-lang=\"\">/collections</code> endpoints. The functionality remains identical, only the terminology has changed. Legacy collections endpoints are deprecated but will continue to  work. We recommend migrating to these new <code class=\"rdmd-code lang- theme-undefined\" data-lang=\"\">/receive</code> endpoints for future compatibility.</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout_warn\" theme=\"🚧\"><span class=\"callout-icon\">🚧</span><h3 class=\"heading heading-3 header-scroll\"><div class=\"heading-anchor anchor waypoint\" id=\"cancellation-status\"></div><div class=\"heading-text\">Cancellation status</div><a aria-label=\"Skip link to Cancellation status\" class=\"heading-anchor-icon fa fa-regular fa-anchor\" href=\"#cancellation-status\"></a></h3><p>You can only cancel a receive when it&#x27;s in <code class=\"rdmd-code lang- theme-undefined\" data-lang=\"\">pending</code> or <code class=\"rdmd-code lang- theme-undefined\" data-lang=\"\">processing</code> state.  If we receive the collection after it&#x27;s cancelled a refund is triggered for the receive.</p></blockquote>"
